From: shadaytree <82917003+shadaytree@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:36:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tools): add metric tap-drill and clearance drills, a 3
 mm ball and a 6 mm bull nose to the catalog

The starter catalog gets 16 tools: BN-0300, BB-0600-R1, and a tap drill
and a clearance drill (ISO 273 medium) for each coarse thread M3-M12.
Each tool goes into its family in diameter order. The cutting data
follows the catalog's own rows (docs/decisions/3036-metric-catalog.md).
Drill flute lengths are on a 0.5 mm step, so the spun holder stacks
bit-identically to the cylinder.

Fixes #3036

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
